{
	"nodes":[
		{"id":"cba-g1","type":"group","x":0,"y":400,"width":1510,"height":1200,"label":"1 · 统计口径：钱记在哪里","color":"5"},
		{"id":"cba-g2","type":"group","x":1750,"y":400,"width":1510,"height":1200,"label":"2 · 规模变化：测量与解释","color":"5"},
		{"id":"cba-g3","type":"group","x":3500,"y":400,"width":1510,"height":1200,"label":"3 · 部门判断：为何与如何介入","color":"4"},
		{"id":"cba-g4","type":"group","x":0,"y":1900,"width":1510,"height":1200,"label":"4 · 政府投资：合同、付费与风险","color":"4"},
		{"id":"cba-g5","type":"group","x":1750,"y":1900,"width":1510,"height":1200,"label":"5 · 项目基准：改变什么、计入谁","color":"6"},
		{"id":"cba-g6","type":"group","x":3500,"y":1900,"width":1510,"height":1200,"label":"6 · 资源账户：估值与避免重复","color":"6"},
		{"id":"cba-g7","type":"group","x":0,"y":3400,"width":1510,"height":1200,"label":"7 · 非市场效益：时间与偏好证据","color":"3"},
		{"id":"cba-g8","type":"group","x":1750,"y":3400,"width":1510,"height":1200,"label":"8 · 风险：安全收益与不确定结果","color":"3"},
		{"id":"cba-g9","type":"group","x":3500,"y":3400,"width":1510,"height":1200,"label":"9 · 时间与选择：现值、边界和替代","color":"2"},
		{"id":"cba-header","type":"text","x":0,"y":0,"width":5010,"height":260,"color":"5","text":"# 公共支出与成本—收益分析\n\n[[02_Economy/02_public finance财政学/02_公共支出与项目评价|从完整课程开始]] · [[02_Economy/02_public finance财政学/02_公共支出与项目评价#6. 完整数例：一项两年期桥梁改善|两年桥梁案例]]\n\n每行从左向右，按 1 → 9 阅读：口径 → 规模机制 → 部门判断 → 投资安排 → 基准范围 → 资源账户 → 非市场效益 → 风险 → 贴现与选择。点击短卡打开单一知识对象；颜色区分问题领域，不表示掌握程度。\n<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\nRead left to right across each row, from measurement and intervention to project accounts, valuation, risk and choice. Each short card opens one knowledge object; colours identify question areas, not mastery.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->"},
		{"id":"exp001","type":"text","x":30,"y":470,"width":350,"height":270,"text":"## [[财政支出]]\n\n政府配置资金的过程及其按明确口径计量的支出结果。\n<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\nGovernment allocation of funds and expenditure measured within a stated perimeter.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->"},
		{"id":"exp002","type":"text","x":580,"y":470,"width":350,"height":270,"text":"## [[财政支出分类]]\n\n功能问服务什么目标；经济分类问发生什么交易。\n<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\nFunction identifies purpose; economic classification identifies the transaction.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->"},
		{"id":"exp005","type":"text","x":1130,"y":470,"width":350,"height":270,"text":"## [[预算支出与决算支出]]\n\n计划授权与执行结果分开；差额本身不说明效率。\n<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\nSeparate authorised plans from outturns; the gap alone does not establish efficiency.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->"},
		{"id":"exp003","type":"text","x":30,"y":860,"width":350,"height":270,"text":"## [[购买支出与转移支出]]\n\n取得商品服务与无直接对价转移，是不同交易。\n<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\nAcquiring goods or services differs from transferring funds without a direct counterpart.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->"},
		{"id":"exp004","type":"text","x":580,"y":860,"width":350,"height":270,"text":"## [[经常支出与资本支出]]\n\n日常运行与资本交易按制度口径区分，不只看付款大小。\n<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\nSeparate current operations and capital transactions using the stated accounting rules.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->"},
		{"id":"exp013","type":"text","x":1130,"y":860,"width":350,"height":270,"text":"## [[GFS费用与支出]]\n\n费用、非金融资产净投资与融资账户不能混同。\n<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\nDistinguish expense, net investment in nonfinancial assets and financing.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->"},
		{"id":"bridge1","type":"text","x":30,"y":1250,"width":1450,"height":270,"color":"5","text":"### 同一教育目标，可以有不同交易\n\n教师工资、校舍购置与助学金不因用途相同就具有相同资源含义。先固定部门、交易、时期和计价范围，再比较支出数。\n<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\nTeacher pay, buildings and grants share an educational purpose but have different resource implications. Fix the sector, transaction, period and price basis before comparing expenditure.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->\n\n[[02_Economy/02_public finance财政学/02_公共支出与项目评价#1. 先问支出数字量的是什么|回到口径辨析]]"},
		{"id":"exp006","type":"text","x":1780,"y":470,"width":350,"height":270,"text":"## [[财政支出占比]]\n\n支出除以同口径 GDP；份额与支出总量回答不同问题。\n<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\nSpending relative to consistent GDP measures a share, not the spending total.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->"},
		{"id":"exp007","type":"text","x":2330,"y":470,"width":350,"height":270,"text":"## [[财政支出增长率]]\n\n比较自身基期；支出增加仍可能伴随 GDP 占比下降。\n<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\nGrowth uses spending's own base; an increase can coexist with a falling GDP share.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->"},
		{"id":"exp008","type":"text","x":2880,"y":470,"width":350,"height":270,"text":"## [[财政支出边际倾向]]\n\n支出增量与 GDP 增量之比，不是政策乘数。\n<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\nThe spending-to-GDP increment ratio is not a fiscal multiplier.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->"},
		{"id":"exp009","type":"text","x":1780,"y":860,"width":350,"height":270,"text":"## [[财政支出弹性]]\n\n比较相对增长；两期比率本身不识别因果机制。\n<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\nRelative growth rates describe responsiveness without establishing causation.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->"},
		{"id":"exp010","type":"text","x":2330,"y":860,"width":350,"height":270,"text":"## [[瓦格纳假说]]\n\n发展可能扩大公共活动需求，须检验历史范围和机制。\n<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\nDevelopment may expand demand for public activities; scope and mechanisms need evidence.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->"},
		{"id":"exp011","type":"text","x":2880,"y":860,"width":350,"height":270,"text":"## [[财政支出的替代效应]]\n\n重大冲击可能改变可接受税负与公共支出水平。\n<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\nMajor disturbances may shift accepted taxation and expenditure levels.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->"},
		{"id":"exp012","type":"text","x":1780,"y":1250,"width":350,"height":270,"text":"## [[发展阶段与财政支出]]\n\n不同阶段的公共需求和任务变化，不是各国必经定律。\n<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\nPublic needs may change with development stages; no universal trajectory is guaranteed.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->"},
		{"id":"bridge2","type":"text","x":2330,"y":1250,"width":900,"height":270,"color":"5","text":"### 从描述转向解释\n\nG：100 → 110；Y：1000 → 1200。支出增 10%，份额却从 10% 降到约 9.17%；增量比 0.05，增长率比 0.5。历史假说还需要额外证据。\n<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\nSpending grows by 10% while its GDP share falls to about 9.17%. The increment ratio is 0.05 and the growth-rate ratio 0.5; explaining either requires further evidence.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->"},
		{"id":"shared-rationale","type":"text","x":3530,"y":470,"width":350,"height":270,"text":"## [[政府干预的效率与分配理由|效率与分配理由]]\n\n先区分激励或信息缺口与社会目标，再比较干预工具。\n<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\nSeparate efficiency gaps from distributive objectives before comparing instruments.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->"},
		{"id":"shared-roles","type":"text","x":4080,"y":470,"width":350,"height":270,"text":"## [[公共品的筹资、生产与治理|筹资、生产与治理]]\n\n政府筹资不要求政府亲自生产；合同与监督也需安排。\n<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\nPublic financing need not mean public production; contracts and oversight still matter.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->"},
		{"id":"exp030","type":"text","x":4630,"y":470,"width":350,"height":270,"text":"## [[基础研究]]\n\n以获得新的基础知识为目标，不预设特定应用。\n<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\nSeek new foundational knowledge without a particular application in view.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->"},
		{"id":"exp031","type":"text","x":3530,"y":860,"width":350,"height":270,"text":"## [[卫生筹资与服务提供]]\n\n资金如何筹集、统筹和支付，不同于谁实际提供诊疗。\n<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\nRaising, pooling and paying funds differs from delivering care.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->"},
		{"id":"elas001","type":"text","x":4080,"y":860,"width":350,"height":270,"text":"## [[价格弹性与总收益]]\n\n沿固定需求降价，缺乏弹性时销售收入减少；收入不是利润。\n<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\nOn fixed inelastic demand, a price cut lowers sales revenue, not necessarily profit.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->"},
		{"id":"bridge3","type":"text","x":3530,"y":1250,"width":1450,"height":270,"color":"4","text":"### 部门名称不能代替机制\n\n国防服务与军用投入分开；教育和文化的私人收益、未计价外溢分开；医疗的信息、竞争与公平问题分开。先确定具体服务与行为，再评价工具。\n<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\nDistinguish defence services from inputs, private educational or cultural benefits from unpriced spillovers, and health information, competition and equity problems. Specify services and behaviour before judging instruments.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->\n\n[[02_Economy/02_public finance财政学/02_公共支出与项目评价#3. 用部门支出练习判断干预理由|读部门应用]] · [[02_Economy/02_public finance财政学/02_公共支出与项目评价#农业应用：产量、销售收入与农民处境不是同一个量|读农业应用]]"},
		{"id":"exp020","type":"text","x":30,"y":1970,"width":350,"height":270,"text":"## [[政府投资]]\n\n资本项目形成长期服务能力；投入金额不证明社会收益。\n<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\nCapital projects create lasting service capacity; investment size does not establish benefit.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->"},
		{"id":"exp021","type":"text","x":580,"y":1970,"width":350,"height":270,"text":"## [[政府和社会资本合作|PPP：政府和社会资本合作]]\n\n长期合同配置私人管理责任、风险与绩效报酬。\n<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\nA long-term contract assigns private responsibilities, risks and performance-linked pay.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->"},
		{"id":"exp022","type":"text","x":1130,"y":1970,"width":350,"height":270,"text":"## [[项目融资与付费来源]]\n\n先筹集建设资金，仍需说明以后由谁付费。\n<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\nRaising construction capital leaves the question of who ultimately pays.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->"},
		{"id":"exp023","type":"text","x":580,"y":2360,"width":350,"height":270,"text":"## [[PPP风险分配]]\n\n逐项比较控制、减缓和承受能力，不以转移最多为目标。\n<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\nCompare control, mitigation and bearing capacity, not maximum private risk transfer.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->"},
		{"id":"bridge4","type":"text","x":30,"y":2750,"width":1450,"height":270,"color":"4","text":"### 融资到位，不等于项目值得\n\n借款 70 加权益 30 可以筹齐初始 100，却没有创造运营收入。政府以后按绩效付款仍是公共承诺；ABS 是融资工具，不能单凭名称认定 PPP。\n<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\nDebt of 70 plus equity of 30 raises 100 without creating operating revenue. Later government payments remain commitments; securitisation alone does not establish a PPP.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->\n\n[[02_Economy/02_public finance财政学/02_公共支出与项目评价#4. 政府投资：先确定项目，再安排融资与责任|读投资与合同安排]]"},
		{"id":"cba002","type":"text","x":1780,"y":1970,"width":350,"height":270,"text":"## [[公共项目反事实]]\n\n不实施待评方案时会怎样？基准不一定保持现状不变。\n<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\nWhat happens without the proposal? The baseline need not freeze current conditions.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->"},
		{"id":"cba003","type":"text","x":2330,"y":1970,"width":350,"height":270,"text":"## [[公共项目评价范围]]\n\n明确哪些人、地区、时期和影响进入社会账户。\n<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\nState whose impacts, which locations and what horizon enter the social account.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->"},
		{"id":"cba009","type":"text","x":2880,"y":1970,"width":350,"height":270,"text":"## [[项目投入产出与结果]]\n\n花了多少、提供什么和改善什么，是三个不同层次。\n<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\nResources used, services delivered and outcomes improved are distinct levels.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->"},
		{"id":"cba001","type":"text","x":2330,"y":2360,"width":350,"height":270,"text":"## [[成本—收益分析]]\n\n在明确基准与范围内比较方案的社会效益和成本。\n<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\nCompare social benefits and costs within an explicit baseline and scope.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->"},
		{"id":"bridge5","type":"text","x":1780,"y":2750,"width":1450,"height":270,"color":"6","text":"### 桥梁的比较对象是渡运基准\n\n先预测有桥与无桥两种情形，再比较出行、时间、风险与资源差额。桥梁本身是产出；便利和安全改善才是待估结果。\n<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\nForecast both bridge and ferry-baseline cases before comparing trips, time, risk and resources. The bridge is an output; improved access and safety are outcomes to value.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->\n\n[[02_Economy/02_public finance财政学/02_公共支出与项目评价#5. 把支出变成可评价的项目|读评价起点]]"},
		{"id":"cba004","type":"text","x":3530,"y":1970,"width":350,"height":270,"text":"## [[财务与社会评价]]\n\n经营者收付款与评价范围内的社会得失，不是同一张账。\n<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\nOperator cash payments and receipts differ from social gains and losses.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->"},
		{"id":"cba005","type":"text","x":4080,"y":1970,"width":350,"height":270,"text":"## [[社会机会成本]]\n\n项目占用资源所放弃的最佳可行用途价值。\n<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\nThe value of the best feasible alternative use forgone by project resources.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->"},
		{"id":"cba006","type":"text","x":4630,"y":1970,"width":350,"height":270,"text":"## [[公共项目影子估值]]\n\n市场价格不能充分反映社会价值时，核对并调整估值。\n<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\nCheck and adjust valuation when market prices do not adequately reflect social value.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->"},
		{"id":"shared-transfer","type":"text","x":3530,"y":2360,"width":350,"height":270,"text":"## [[转移支付核算]]\n\n同一范围内付款与收款对齐；真实资源成本只计一次。\n<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\nReconcile payer and recipient entries within one scope; count resource costs once.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->"},
		{"id":"cba007","type":"text","x":4080,"y":2360,"width":350,"height":270,"text":"## [[收益流与资产增值]]\n\n资产升值可能资本化已计入的未来便利，不能重复相加。\n<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\nAppreciation may capitalise benefits already counted in the future service stream.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->"},
		{"id":"cba011","type":"text","x":4630,"y":2360,"width":350,"height":270,"text":"## [[诱发需求半数法]]\n\n新增使用者沿需求曲线获益；线性条件下用三角形面积。\n<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\nInduced users gain along the demand curve; linearity yields the triangle formula.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->"},
		{"id":"bridge6","type":"text","x":3530,"y":2750,"width":1450,"height":270,"color":"6","text":"### 把资源、转移和效益来源分清\n\n工资付款不等于全部资源损失；通行费需核对两边账户；通勤便利与由它带来的房价升值不能重复计价。需求变化时，新增出行也不能照搬原使用者的全部收益。\n<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\nReconcile wages and tolls with resources and counterpart entries. Avoid counting both commuting benefits and their capitalisation, and value induced trips separately from existing users.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->"},
		{"id":"cba020","type":"text","x":30,"y":3470,"width":350,"height":270,"text":"## [[非市场估值]]\n\n缺少直接交易价格，仍可研究明确变化的福利价值。\n<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\nA specified welfare change can be valued even without a direct market price.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->"},
		{"id":"cba023","type":"text","x":580,"y":3470,"width":350,"height":270,"text":"## [[显示偏好估值]]\n\n从实际选择识别权衡，需要可辩护的行为与识别条件。\n<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\nInfer trade-offs from observed choices under defensible behavioural and identification conditions.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->"},
		{"id":"cba024","type":"text","x":1130,"y":3470,"width":350,"height":270,"text":"## [[享乐价格估值]]\n\n价格函数的属性梯度，可在条件下反映局部边际支付意愿。\n<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\nA hedonic price gradient can reveal local marginal willingness to pay under conditions.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->"},
		{"id":"cba021","type":"text","x":30,"y":3860,"width":350,"height":270,"text":"## [[时间节约价值]]\n\n对指定活动时间节约的边际支付意愿，不是每小时统一价格。\n<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\nMarginal willingness to pay for specified time savings is not one universal hourly price.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->"},
		{"id":"cba025","type":"text","x":1130,"y":3860,"width":350,"height":270,"text":"## [[条件估值]]\n\n问卷说明假想改善与支付机制，再询问支付意愿。\n<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\nA survey specifies a hypothetical change and payment mechanism before eliciting willingness to pay.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->"},
		{"id":"cba022","type":"text","x":30,"y":4250,"width":350,"height":270,"text":"## [[工资与时间价值]]\n\n工资映射为时间价值需要工时选择、税收等条件。\n<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\nMapping wages into time values requires assumptions about work choice, taxes and constraints.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->"},
		{"id":"cba026","type":"text","x":1130,"y":4250,"width":350,"height":270,"text":"## [[条件估值的范围检验]]\n\n比较改善范围变化后的回答；范围扩大不要求价值成比例。\n<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\nTest responses to changed scope without imposing proportional value growth.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->"},
		{"id":"bridge7","type":"text","x":580,"y":4250,"width":350,"height":270,"color":"3","text":"### 估值必须匹配变化\n\n属性、人群、收入与时间单位要一致；局部梯度不能直接代表任意大改善。\n<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\nMatch attributes, population, income and time units; a local gradient does not automatically value a large change.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->"},
		{"id":"cba029","type":"text","x":1780,"y":3470,"width":350,"height":270,"text":"## [[工资风险补偿法]]\n\n在识别条件下，用工资与工作死亡风险的边际权衡估值。\n<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\nUse the marginal wage–mortality-risk trade-off subject to identification conditions.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->"},
		{"id":"cba027","type":"text","x":2330,"y":3470,"width":350,"height":270,"text":"## [[统计生命价值]]\n\n每单位死亡概率降低的边际支付意愿，不是给指定生命定价。\n<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\nMarginal willingness to pay per unit of mortality-probability reduction is not the price of an identified life.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->"},
		{"id":"cba028","type":"text","x":2880,"y":3470,"width":350,"height":270,"text":"## [[死亡风险降低收益]]\n\n按人群匹配风险变化与支付意愿，再用一致单位加总。\n<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\nMatch risk changes and willingness to pay by population, then aggregate consistent units.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->"},
		{"id":"cba035","type":"text","x":1780,"y":3860,"width":350,"height":270,"text":"## [[期望净收益准则]]\n\n按明确概率比较平均净收益；这种排序需要相应评价条件。\n<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\nRank mean net benefits using stated probabilities and an appropriate evaluation criterion.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->"},
		{"id":"cba036","type":"text","x":2330,"y":3860,"width":350,"height":270,"text":"## [[风险的确定性等价]]\n\n指定财富背景与效用后，找偏好上等价的确定结果。\n<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\nGiven background wealth and utility, find a sure outcome equivalent in preference.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->"},
		{"id":"cba030","type":"text","x":2880,"y":3860,"width":350,"height":270,"text":"## [[生命收入法的估值边界]]\n\n劳动收入损失与风险支付意愿不同；退休不意味着生命价值为零。\n<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\nLost earnings differ from risk willingness to pay; retirement does not imply zero value.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->"},
		{"id":"shared-sensitivity","type":"text","x":1780,"y":4250,"width":350,"height":270,"text":"## [[敏感性、情景与模拟]]\n\n改参数、比较组合情景、按概率模拟，是三种不同操作。\n<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\nParameter changes, scenario comparisons and probabilistic simulation are distinct operations.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->"},
		{"id":"bridge8","type":"text","x":2330,"y":4250,"width":900,"height":270,"color":"3","text":"### 两种风险问题不要合并\n\n安全效益问人们愿为死亡概率降低付多少；项目不确定性问未来需求等结果有多大概率、决策者怎样评价风险。乐观和悲观情景本身不提供概率。\n<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\nSafety valuation asks willingness to pay for lower mortality risk. Project uncertainty concerns outcome probabilities and risk preferences; optimistic and pessimistic scenarios do not supply probabilities.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->"},
		{"id":"cba031","type":"text","x":3530,"y":3470,"width":350,"height":270,"text":"## [[社会贴现率]]\n\n把不同日期社会成本效益换成同一时点价值的贴现口径。\n<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\nSpecify the discount rate used to compare dated social costs and benefits.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->"},
		{"id":"cba032","type":"text","x":4080,"y":3470,"width":350,"height":270,"text":"## [[社会时间偏好率]]\n\n从跨期社会消费取舍说明贴现率，参数和条件必须明示。\n<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\nGround discounting in intertemporal social consumption choices with explicit assumptions.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->"},
		{"id":"cba033","type":"text","x":4630,"y":3470,"width":350,"height":270,"text":"## [[社会资本机会成本]]\n\n公共项目挤出的资本用途可能牺牲真实社会回报。\n<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\nDisplaced capital uses may carry forgone real social returns.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->"},
		{"id":"shared-pv","type":"text","x":3530,"y":3860,"width":350,"height":270,"text":"## [[现金流同点折现加总]]\n\n先用一致贴现因子移到同一时点，再加总。\n<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\nApply consistent discount factors to a common date before summing.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->"},
		{"id":"cba034","type":"text","x":4080,"y":3860,"width":350,"height":270,"text":"## [[社会贴现与代际评价]]\n\n纯时间偏好、消费增长与跨代分配判断应分别说明。\n<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\nSeparate pure time preference, consumption growth and intergenerational distribution.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->"},
		{"id":"cba013","type":"text","x":4630,"y":3860,"width":350,"height":270,"text":"## [[收益成本比]]\n\n折现收益除以折现成本；分类与规模会影响比率及排序。\n<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\nDiscounted benefits over costs depend on classification and do not settle scale comparisons.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->"},
		{"id":"bridge9","type":"text","x":3530,"y":4250,"width":350,"height":270,"color":"2","text":"### 两年桥梁：按增量复算\n\n今天 −100；两次年末各 +60；实际贴现率 5%。净现值约 11.56。\n<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\nWith −100 now and +60 at each year-end, a 5% real rate gives NPV ≈ 11.56.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->\n\n[[02_Economy/02_public finance财政学/02_公共支出与项目评价#6. 完整数例：一项两年期桥梁改善|打开完整假设与临界值]]"},
		{"id":"cba010","type":"text","x":4080,"y":4250,"width":350,"height":270,"text":"## [[公共项目净现值边界]]\n\n正净现值仍须检查替代方案、遗漏影响、分配与可实施性。\n<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\nPositive NPV still requires alternatives, omitted impacts, distribution and feasibility to be assessed.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->"},
		{"id":"cba008","type":"text","x":4630,"y":4250,"width":350,"height":270,"text":"## [[成本效果分析]]\n\n不能充分货币化时，在结果可比条件下比较达标成本。\n<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\nWhen monetisation is limited, compare costs for sufficiently comparable outcomes or targets.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->"}
	],
